monarch, he immediately issued out, and went to the inner apartment of his mother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"20535364b5293145cac55cfb11acd3c58237c8f773d6a700d11a584bcdf49d85","compact":"f0b89eba7c7d2dca0cecb7db5aa520c077fc97ccbd1820150d469da285cb56e4","nasal":"c3d71875df28d1fd81a6d8d8a891a3a1a24dbc5bcea231705462e6670b2554a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":30,"english":"There, Rāma found his mother in the temple, clad in silk, adoring the gods, and silently praying for his royal luck.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"85adb6963327a99b61b99b10555f6a802e2db28b41c33f53431cbfe900801169","compact":"fbe3b904d3984aa4a85a70ea027223bc08366c8749a3fc190fedffd9ca5a1042","nasal":"fbe3b904d3984aa4a85a70ea027223bc08366c8749a3fc190fedffd9ca5a1042"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":31,"english":"There, hearing of the welcome installation of Råma, had already come Sumitrā, and Lakşmaņa and Sītā summoned (by Kausalyā).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"607146d15bf3e0e111edd9394207a17eee769e7c0a2fef827e70cc1c816fbb86","compact":"0255697451cb1b56062b277ca5061daf9e3d00d4897257cb7bb782ef1621f7e2","nasal":"0255697451cb1b56062b277ca5061daf9e3d00d4897257cb7bb782ef1621f7e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":32,"english":"Hearing of the installation of his son in the office of heir-apparent during the influence of the Puşya at that time, tended by Sumitrā and Sita and Laksmana, there stood Kausalya, meditating the (triune) person Janārdana, through suspension of breath.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"739bd707d77d511961b8b80221e347c45d724dd6890cc8bf496b73940c6ae066","compact":"51c4e3bdf2976ce213caea59cb03691cf1d963ba8c6e76644d162da7f6ee28e9","nasal":"51c4e3bdf2976ce213caea59cb03691cf1d963ba8c6e76644d162da7f6ee28e9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":33,"english":"Hearing of the installation of his son in the office of heir-apparent during the influence of the Puşya at that time, tended by Sumitrā and Sita and Laksmana, there stood Kausalya, meditating the (triune) person Janārdana, through suspension of breath.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.765,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4729259a8b1c5b705cd1d1582453e883e7abae8065d159e7528adae219898ca8","compact":"e79cf54cb216ea22b7efc055a6500de9da6ad678e8a2e9f9d9864cc630c24baa","nasal":"6d3e992cfa7debe926f0d3dfc9ccc5da60df82e235067d6f3400b27e39b5180a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":34,"english":"Rāma, approaching and saluting her engaged in auspicious observance, addressed her in excellent words, cheering her up, O mother, by my father have I been appointed to the task of governing the people. And, agreeably to the desire of my father, to morrow will take place my installation; To night Sītā will fast along with me, the priests have said thus, and this also has been declared by my father.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.784,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d699639510410cbcd885eb6045a74218d460191832ef80274fe5c7ea760f7fe","compact":"4634dbeb0a451164b3e3d830c3e7fc6fd5e5d921e88e4cc475e0bf33c450f3d0","nasal":"4634dbeb0a451164b3e3d830c3e7fc6fd5e5d921e88e4cc475e0bf33c450f3d0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":35,"english":"Rāma, approaching and saluting her engaged in auspicious observance, addressed her in excellent words, cheering her up, O mother, by my father have I been appointed to the task of governing the people. And, agreeably to the desire of my father, to morrow will take place my installation; To night Sītā will fast along with me, the priests have said thus, and this also has been declared by my father.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004035","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"acde58f339d040cee9a4decc015193856b4e2a889d9b47a2d8eae1e414206963","compact":"584498e1d8924adfd75e401c37bcfba1b928a3b577a43858ce56d5e2bb9e5470","nasal":"b23705ce1778a09778486c8875032ddce22e86867ac36a91bb5cfa677b783f1a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-36","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":36,"english":"Rāma, approaching and saluting her engaged in auspicious observance, addressed her in excellent words, cheering her up, O mother, by my father have I been appointed to the task of governing the people. And, agreeably to the desire of my father, to morrow will take place my installation; To night Sītā will fast along with me, the priests have said thus, and this also has been declared by my father.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.655,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004036","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"39cc6e9ea9a6f8078345c43a2a9360f773540ba6e476fd2d8c83f5ad20fe6af6","compact":"5e0955c5d61596a6227bdd3d445a52973b7efd85e3dcd1f956d4b3676ffda81b","nasal":"5e0955c5d61596a6227bdd3d445a52973b7efd85e3dcd1f956d4b3676ffda81b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-37","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":37,"english":"Do you therefore even today provide those necessary auspicious things that will be required Hur myself and Vaidehi on the occasion of the coming installation.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004037","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"752ea444420f028ac06e0ce5018e8be46243133e49093b206498cbedd3b5cba3","compact":"fcb658b48da1a5ef1c78c3aaa2f88d50f486e1c9d511b35c62a72497e39865c8","nasal":"251aa44f5ff841377236983417817de2d6b8b05d4e03535b38ba0f4506557c38"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-38","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":38,"english":"Hearing of that for which she had ever wished, Kausalya, her voice choking with the vapour begot of delight, addressed Rāma, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.683,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004038","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cd870563756260496111b9fb9dd34a5b304be2e2abaafe63c97dc9fccd5c716f","compact":"925ffaac1124e2782c257fe0108f1e1f2bc488a941dece038844480900b1781a","nasal":"42a54d4c4e880c5d1dd25ceed84adbf72d639e80dd05ef59254a2a618e29c52a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-39","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":39,"english":"Rāma, my child, be you long-lived, and may your enemies find destruction! Furnished with this good fortune, do you gladden Sumitra's as well as my own relatives.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004039","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"977e5228acc67b0331bfe79e105fb501b8ee25883455c951fbac312af6459173","compact":"efff4edd8f8c0e644153e8e547a16d443a82af0f6f0cf46ac10fad3da91b4a0e","nasal":"39def6fa982757ddc44570ba3be4077eda55618256869367eabef54197e13667"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-40","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":40,"english":"Oh! you was born under an auspicious star: you have, O son, by your virtues gratified your sire Dasaratha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.796,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004040","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6fe9144abfe0a484361646549c23e4b280f7a2ebb3d7646810618f2189128bb9","compact":"25f1d4a7b1376202b5a03756a101c192aa10d8767e27dfe27b8d096ab29ee868","nasal":"25f1d4a7b1376202b5a03756a101c192aa10d8767e27dfe27b8d096ab29ee868"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-4-41","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":4,"verse":41,"english":"Ah! not unfruitful has proved my disinterested observance of vow to the lotus-eyed person, for this royal fortune of the Ikşvāku race shall rest upon you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-4-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2004041","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"03a58de8eefb46e105f71a69ec552289b28c99ccffcf8fbd74da17faf4376207","compact":"371f4636159776fbae00926a2299919f25c93e40f1c7abb21ec4ccd1189aaa5b","na